    apply: { situation: ['Listen to Nao\'s short invitation before the walk. Identify the meeting plan and what Leo can borrow.', '散歩の前の、ナオの短い誘いを聞きましょう。待ち合わせの予定と、レオが借りられるものを聞き取りましょう。'], text: '<p>Hi Leo. Let\'s meet at the cafe entrance at ten on Saturday. Claire says you can borrow her camera. I prefer the quiet path by the river. We can practise taking photos there. Bring some water. If it rains, let\'s stay at the cafe and look at photos instead.</p>', questions: [['When and where will they meet?', 'Saturday at ten, at the cafe entrance.'], ['Whose camera can Leo borrow?', 'Claire\'s camera.'], ['Which path does Nao prefer?', 'The quiet path by the river.'], ['What will they do if it rains?', 'Stay at the cafe and look at photos.']] },
    choose: [['Let\'s (meet / meeting) at ten.', 'meet'], ['Why don\'t we (walk / walking) by the river?', 'walk'], ['Could I (borrow / lend) a camera from Claire?', 'borrow'], ['Keep the camera (still / stillness).', 'still'], ['I prefer the quiet (path / passing).', 'path'], ['I took a photo of my shoes by (accident / accidental).', 'accident']],
    choices: [['"Let\'s meet at ten, not nine." Which time is confirmed?', 'Nine', 'Ten', 'B'], ['"Claire can lend you her camera." What can Leo do?', 'Borrow Claire\'s camera', 'Keep it permanently', 'A'], ['"Keep the camera still." What should Leo do?', 'Shake it quickly', 'Avoid moving it', 'B'], ['"If it rains, we will stay at the cafe." What changes?', 'The activity changes to looking at photos indoors.', 'They must walk by the river in the rain.', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Leo beside the river. Your tutor reads Nao\'s camera advice, then plays Claire when you return her camera. Explain the advice and the funny mistake you made.', 'あなたは川のそばにいるレオ役です。講師はナオの助言を読んでから、カメラを返すときのクレア役になります。聞いた助言と、うっかりしてしまったことを説明しましょう。'], task: ['Listen for where to stand, what to photograph, and how to hold the camera. Tell Claire the details, explain that you photographed your shoes by accident, and say what you enjoyed.', '立つ場所、撮るもの、カメラの持ち方を聞き取りましょう。クレアに内容を伝え、うっかり靴を撮ったことと、楽しかったことを話しましょう。'], roles: ['Claire', 'Leo'], text: '<p>Leo, stand on the wide path, away from the cyclists. Try a lower angle to photograph the bridge. Hold the camera still with both hands. You do not need the flash outside. After that, let\'s sit on the bench and choose our favourite picture.</p>', lines: ['Welcome back, Leo. Where did Nao tell you to stand?', 'What did she suggest photographing?', 'How did she tell you to hold the camera? Did you need the flash?', 'What did you plan to do on the bench?', 'Nao mentioned a funny photo. What happened?', 'What did you enjoy about the afternoon?'], evidence: 'Wide path away from cyclists, lower angle for bridge, camera still with both hands, no flash outside, bench to choose favourite picture. Shoe photo is given in the situation, not a hidden listening answer. Separate listening evidence from grammar and let the learner request a repeated sentence.', useful: ['She suggested ...', 'She told me to ...', 'I did not need ...', 'After that, we ...', 'I photographed ... by accident.', 'Could you repeat that part?'] },
    topics: [['TRYING A HOBBY', ['What hobby would you like to try?', 'What would you ask a beginner?', 'How could you help them enjoy it?']], ['A RELAXING AFTERNOON', ['Would you choose a walk or a cafe?', 'What would you bring?', 'What would you do if the weather changed?']], ['LEARNING TOGETHER', ['How can you give a short suggestion?', 'How can you ask for a demonstration?', 'What can you say after a harmless mistake?']]],
    trivia: ['Borrow and lend describe the same temporary exchange from opposite sides. Leo borrows a camera from Claire; Claire lends a camera to Leo. "Can you borrow me a camera?" does not mean "Can you lend me your camera?"', 'borrow と lend は、一時的な貸し借りを反対の立場から表します。レオはクレアから borrow（借りる）し、クレアはレオに lend（貸す）します。「あなたのカメラを貸して」と言うなら Can you lend me your camera? です。'], triviaQuestion: ['Leo receives Claire\'s camera for the afternoon. Does he borrow it or lend it?', 'He borrows it.'],
